---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<Legal
  title="Privacy"
  description={`How ${site.name} handles the personal information you give us through this website.`}
  lede="What we collect through this website, why, and what you can ask us to do with it. Written to be read."
>
  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    This website is run by {site.legalEntity}, doing business as {site.name}, of {site.legalAddress}. For anything to
    do with your information, write to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> or call {site.phoneDisplay}.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>What you type into the contact form: your name, work email, company, the services you ticked and your message.</li>
    <li>Emails you send us, and our replies.</li>
    <li>Basic server logs kept by our hosting provider, such as IP address and the pages requested.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We don't buy contact lists, and we don't collect anything about you from other sources.</p>

  <h2>Why we collect it</h2>
  <p>To reply to you, prepare for a call you asked for, and keep a record of our conversation.</p>
  <p>We won't add you to a mailing list because you filled in the form.</p>

  <h2>Who sees it</h2>
  <p>
    The {site.name} team, and the services we use to run the site, the contact form and our email. We don't sell or
    rent your information to anyone.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    If we don't end up working together, we delete your enquiry after 12 months. If we do, the records are kept for as
    long as the law requires for business records.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
  <p>This site sets no advertising or tracking cookies.</p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask for a copy of what we hold about you, ask us to correct it, or ask us to delete it. Email{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> or call {site.phoneDisplay}, and we'll act on it within 30 days.
  </p>

  <h2>Information in client projects</h2>
  <p>
    When we work for a client, any personal data in their systems is handled under our contract with that client, and
    this page doesn't cover it.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If this page changes, the date at the top changes with it.</p>
</Legal>
